cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "The Compositional Depth Decay is a Dispatch Tax"
message: "If you reference this work, please cite as below."
type: "report"
version: "0.1"
authors:
  - family-names: "Dovzak"
    given-names: "Juan Cruz"
    email: "juandovzak@gmail.com"
date-released: "2026-04-24"
url: "https://github.com/OriginalKazdov/treemote-report"
abstract: >-
  Compositional depth decay in neural networks behaves like an
  exponential dispatch tax — a multiplicative cost per depth step
  on out-of-distribution composition. A parse-given tree-recursive
  evaluator with a shared typed-bilinear cell (TreeMoTE) eliminates
  this decay across modular RPN, Boolean RPN, and infix arithmetic
  task families, while a same-structure control with a generic MLP
  cell does not. The report covers a seven-gate validation battery
  including cell audits, shape transfer, parse corruption, and
  multi-seed checks.
keywords:
  - compositional generalization
  - depth extrapolation
  - tree-recursive networks
  - bilinear operators
  - structured reasoning
  - parse-given evaluation
